                        ],
                        "form": "huurlinkjes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb4da870-c916-3256-b940-80a15e683506",
                        "entry_id": "19cd73d0-614d-3453-bf36-62b3a9e89548",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand die tegen betaling krijgsdienst verricht in vreemde dienst"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "517e604b-3da2-4308-bed5-78d2151e93a2",
                                "sense_id": "bb4da870-c916-3256-b940-80a15e683506",
                                "text": "De huurlingen sloegen aan het muiten toen hun soldij niet op tijd betaald werd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d43709e-1b83-4b49-83dc-d7cc9ffb8c74",
                                "sense_id": "bb4da870-c916-3256-b940-80a15e683506",
                                "text": "Volgens de overlevering vluchtten meisjes uit Plancher-Les-Mines gedurende de Dertigjarige Oorlog (1618-1648) de bossen in om te ontkomen aan bloeddorstige huurlingen in dienst van de Zweedse bezetter."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1fd85e17-8aae-4da1-8cb3-473e9f91f9ce",
                        "source_entry_id": "19cd73d0-614d-3453-bf36-62b3a9e89548",
                        "source_sense_id": "bb4da870-c916-3256-b940-80a15e683506",
                        "source_sense_description": "iemand die tegen betaling krijgsdienst verricht in vreemde dienst",
                        "target_lang_word": "mercenary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mercenary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c750d0eb-50f2-380b-8283-0d3d6c7076b8",
                                        "entry_id": "edc8bb50-726f-3243-822c-cf70aeaad474",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One motivated by gain, especially monetary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32554ce0-dc7c-4194-9236-d84c6462147c",
                                                "sense_id": "c750d0eb-50f2-380b-8283-0d3d6c7076b8",
                                                "text": "J. Argyrofylus, a mercenary Greek, who came to teach school in Italy, after the sacking of Constantinople by the Turks, used to maintain that Cicero understood neither Philosophy nor Greek"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1025d38-a316-4bd0-8f3e-73d1f6702f8c",
                                                "sense_id": "c750d0eb-50f2-380b-8283-0d3d6c7076b8",
                                                "text": "Such a man emphatically deserves the name of fortune-hunter—a wretch as detestable in society, as destructive of domestic happiness! And if, when marriages are consummated on such plans, there be afterwards between the parties the least appearance of regard, and the common forms of decorum, it is more than can reasonably be expected, and infinitely more than such mercenaries deserve."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "557ef6a2-b17d-42dc-b824-babeab8c0bb8",
                                                "sense_id": "c750d0eb-50f2-380b-8283-0d3d6c7076b8",
                                                "text": "HOSPITAL NUNS./ Louis XVI. wishing to improve the state of the hospitals in France, sent a member of the Academy of Sciences to England, to enquire into the manner in which such establishments were conducted there. The commissioner praised them; but remarked, that two things were wanting; the zeal of the French parochial clergy, and the charity of the hospital nuns. \"We have found, by sorrowful experience,\" said M. Portalis, that mercenaries, without any motive of feeling to attach them constantly to their duty, can never supply the place of persons animated by a spirit of religion,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86905d7c-a7ba-48ca-b10a-59be78dd565c",
                                                "sense_id": "c750d0eb-50f2-380b-8283-0d3d6c7076b8",
                                                "text": "In the higher ranks of life especially, it is, unhappily, a very common practice to commit to hired mercenaries, that important duty which nature at once commands and enables the mother to perform; that of suckling her infant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d547348-0d1b-48d5-b452-f1ea2c752e64",
                                                "sense_id": "c750d0eb-50f2-380b-8283-0d3d6c7076b8",
                                                "text": "For that is the characteristic of a mercenary, who acts through interest, rather than of an affectionate child who acts through love. There is a great difference, say they, between the service of a slave, the service of a mercenary or hireling, and the service of a child."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b658a2a-cca5-3b1b-b1bc-ecd6d26ad1d5",
                                        "entry_id": "edc8bb50-726f-3243-822c-cf70aeaad474",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person employed to fight in an armed conflict who is not a member of the state or military group for which they are fighting and whose primary motivation is private gain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1097cdf6-95cc-4277-b62c-39f93399ba04",
                                                "sense_id": "7b658a2a-cca5-3b1b-b1bc-ecd6d26ad1d5",
                                                "text": "He exhorts the emperor to revive the courage of his subjects by the example of manly virtue; to banish luxury from the court and from the camp; to substitute in the place of the Barbarian mercenaries, an army of men interested in the defence of their laws and of their property"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2b0bfbd-c3b6-49aa-b635-984b3b2e0e74",
                                                "sense_id": "7b658a2a-cca5-3b1b-b1bc-ecd6d26ad1d5",
                                                "text": "If a mercenary died, that was one fewer man to pay. Mercenaries were an efficient way to run a military campaign especially in view of the employer's ability to hire and fire when and if the situation demanded"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c92c0398-cdc4-4e9d-9389-05d55b0ba94a",
                                                "sense_id": "7b658a2a-cca5-3b1b-b1bc-ecd6d26ad1d5",
                                                "text": "The combat fatigues worn by the vehicle personnel did not appear to be standard military issue, more similar to what you would expect mercenaries to wear. Mercenaries, loyal to nothing except themselves and their off-shore bank accounts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa29135f-85cc-3c2f-9b29-a0aba8a73cea",
                                        "entry_id": "edc8bb50-726f-3243-822c-cf70aeaad474",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One hired to engage in a figurative battle, as a corporate takeover, a lawsuit, or a political campaign."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mercenary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e1c7e50-0f1a-3bc2-9acb-db043dc10e2e",
                                        "entry_id": "c8949a32-da09-32f3-9931-f13c068039f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Motivated by personal gain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3067903f-2777-443f-a99e-b9d00a526217",
                                                "sense_id": "8e1c7e50-0f1a-3bc2-9acb-db043dc10e2e",
                                                "text": "Success is never so interesting as struggle—not even to the successful, not even to the most mercenary forms of ambition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
